<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is important to note that many nodes are labeled as arid by our
heuristic (see Section <a href="#S3" title="III Arid Node Detection ‣ Practical Mutation Testing at Scale A view from Google" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>), and are not considered for mutation at all.
Furthermore, only a single mutant in a line is ever produced, all others are
not considered. These design decisions proved to be the core of making mutation
testing feasible at very large scale.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Targeted Selection</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The targeted mutation operator selection strategy orders the operators by their
perceived productivity in the mutation AST context, as shown in
Listing <a href="#LST3" title="Listing 3 ‣ IV-B Targeted Selection ‣ IV Mutant Selection Criteria ‣ Practical Mutation Testing at Scale A view from Google" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
