<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">A-A</span>2 </span>Memory and Capacity Functionality</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Often it makes sense to pre-allocate memory for efficiency, when the total size
is known in advance. Mutants in these memory size specifications are not good
test goals; they usually create functionally equivalent code and are not
killable by standard testing methods.</p>
</div>
