<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similar constructs exist in all programming languages, and the heuristic extends to all of these such as <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">std::vector::resize</span>, or
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reserve</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">shrink_to_fit</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">free</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">delete</span>.
These represent a family of common functions of many containers in many
languages, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">std::vector</span> being just a representative example.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Another interesting example are cache prefetch instructions added with SSE,
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prefetch0</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prefetch</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prefetch2</span> and
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prefetchnta</span> accessible with <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">__builtin</span> or
directly by an asm block.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.SS1.SSS2.fig4" class="ltx_figure">
