</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation.</span> This is implemented using AST-level arid node tagging, matching call expressions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Soundness.</span> This heuristic is sound; it uses exact symbols and type
names.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">A-A</span>3 </span>Monitoring Systems</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although it may be debatable whether monitoring logic should be tested or not, developers did not use such mutants productively and instead reported them as being unproductive. Consequently, heuristics mark AST nodes related to monitoring logic as arid.</p>
</div>
