<section id="A1.SS1.SSS10" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS10.6" class="ltx_text">A-A</span>10 </span>Logical Comparator with Null Child</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When comparing something to <span id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nullptr</span> and its corresponding value in other languages (<span id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NULL</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nil</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">null</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS10.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">None</span>, …),
picking the left (or right, depending where the null value is) is equivalent to
replacing the binary operator with false.</p>
</div>
