</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS11" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS11.6" class="ltx_text">A-A</span>11 </span>Floating Point Equality</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Floating point equality comparison, except for special values such as zero, is mostly meaningless. For a number <span id="A1.SS1.SSS11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">x</span> that is not 0, replacing <span id="A1.SS1.SSS11.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">f() &gt; x</span> with <span id="A1.SS1.SSS11.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">f() &gt;= x</span> is not a good test goal.</p>
</div>
