<section id="A1.SS1.SSS22" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS22.6" class="ltx_text">A-A</span>22 </span>Early Exit Optimizations</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS22.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Linus Torvalds famously states that <span id="A1.SS1.SSS22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"…if you need more than 3 levels
of indentation, you’re screwed anyway, and should fix your program."</span> in the
kernel coding style. While this is sometimes hard to accomplish, having less
things to remember is a good thing, so it is encouraged by the code style to
return early if possible.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS22.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS22.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the following mutant:</p>
</div>
