<p id="A1.SS4.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation.</span> This is implemented using AST-level arid node tagging, matching complex code structures. The triggering condition is that all leaf nodes are a return
statement.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Soundness.</span> This heuristic is not sound, because it relies on the code
style recommendation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS5.6" class="ltx_text">A-D</span>5 </span>Print</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Python2, print is a first-class citizen of the AST; it is not a function that
is called using a <span id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CallExpr</span>(call expression, e.g. function or method invocation). While this is covered by the Low Level API
heuristics, it is worth noting that Python requires handling this differently.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.SS4.SSS5.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS5.fig1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,LSAgfHByaW50ICdleGl0aW5nLi4uJ3w=" download="">⬇</a></div>
