</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation.</span> This is implemented using AST-level arid node tagging, matching expressions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Soundness.</span> This heuristic is not sound.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A1.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">A-E</span> </span><span id="A1.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Go</span></h3>

<section id="A1.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">A-E</span>1 </span>Memory Allocation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Go has a built-in make function to allocate and initialize objects of type
<span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">slice</span>, <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">map</span> or <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">chan</span>. The size parameter is used for specifying the slice
capacity, the map size or the channel buffer capacity. The initial capacity will
be grown by the runtime as needed, so changing it is undetectable by functional
tests. This is a special case of the generic memory and capacity functionality,
but it is worth explicitly mentioning because of the builtin status of this
function and the AST handling.</p>
</div>
